The following code sample shows how you can use Cognitive Services to translate
sentences. The main concept underlying this translation service is that you can post the
sentence you want to translate, according to the key and region where the service was set.
The following code enables you to post a request to the service API:
private static async Task<string> PostAPI(string api, string key, string
region,
string textToTranslate)
{
string result = String.Empty;
using (var client = new HttpClient())
{
using (var request = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Post, api))
{
request.Headers.Add("Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key", key);
request.Headers.Add("Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Region", region);
